PS-twin
Copyright 2026 GremlinNavi

PS-twin is a standalone open-source PowerShell publication, verification, and repository-redundancy utility developed for the Open-Source World Access Project (OSWAP).

The canonical project identity is provider agnostic. The current implementation uses standard Git transport and supports the explicit `git push twin` workflow, but GitHub, GitLab, self-hosted Git services, and future repository providers are deployment surfaces rather than the identity of the project.

Historical repository URLs, filenames, archives, checksums, or compatibility-facing helpers may retain `git-push-twin` or `GitPushTwin` text where renaming would break published references or compatibility. Those occurrences do not imply provider preference.

